1
00:00:04,172 --> 00:00:05,639
My name's Pavi.

2
00:00:05,739 --> 00:00:07,541
And this here is Geet.

3
00:00:08,209 --> 00:00:11,145
Trust me,
the last thing we want is

4
00:00:11,212 --> 00:00:13,381
to be noticed by anyone
in the Brigade.

5
00:00:13,814 --> 00:00:18,352
So the Avatar's cruel reign
over humanity finally ended.

6
00:00:18,452 --> 00:00:22,022
Our ancestors banded together
and created...

7
00:00:22,123 --> 00:00:25,059
the Seven Havens.

8
00:00:28,096 --> 00:00:30,631
That's an unregistered bender!

9
00:00:39,907 --> 00:00:40,941
The Avatar...

10
00:00:42,643 --> 00:00:45,479
You can't have found the Avatar
because...

11
00:00:47,981 --> 00:00:49,217
I already have.

12
00:00:58,826 --> 00:01:00,328
Huh?

13
00:01:00,428 --> 00:01:02,263
Whoa!

14
00:01:21,582 --> 00:01:23,651
Did you see that? I'm awesome!

15
00:01:28,422 --> 00:01:29,590
Good work, Cadets.

16
00:01:29,723 --> 00:01:32,426
Take the rest of the day
and enjoy the festival.

17
00:01:32,526 --> 00:01:34,228
-Off with ya!
-Wanna play hunt the Avatar?

18
00:01:34,295 --> 00:01:35,429
Bet I'm faster than you!

19
00:01:35,563 --> 00:01:37,298
-Only if I'm not it!
-Okay, then you're on!

20
00:01:37,398 --> 00:01:39,032
Winner gets the first Kulfi Pop!

21
00:01:40,533 --> 00:01:42,402
Nisha,
that was reckless.

22
00:01:42,470 --> 00:01:43,771
You absolutely

23
00:01:43,871 --> 00:01:45,602
-cannot bend in public.
-Cannot bend in public.

24
00:01:45,606 --> 00:01:47,808
But these kids are amateurs
compared to me.

25
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:49,877
That is not the point.

26
00:01:49,943 --> 00:01:51,479
Never mind.

27
00:01:51,579 --> 00:01:53,181
I need to get
to the festival ground.

28
00:01:53,281 --> 00:01:55,949
Apparently, there's a ruckus
with some crazed beetles.

29
00:01:56,049 --> 00:01:59,187
Captain Karthik,
can I please go to the festival?

30
00:01:59,287 --> 00:02:00,854
Nisha, you know the answer.

31
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:02,890
I promise I won't bend
a single pebble!

32
00:02:02,990 --> 00:02:05,893
I can't do my job
if I have to keep one eye on you

33
00:02:05,993 --> 00:02:06,994
the entire time.

34
00:02:07,094 --> 00:02:08,662
What's the point
of being the Avatar

35
00:02:08,762 --> 00:02:10,931
if I'm hiding in my room
all the time?!

36
00:02:11,699 --> 00:02:14,568
Your day in the sun will come,
young one.

37
00:02:15,436 --> 00:02:17,438
Just... not today.

38
00:02:30,318 --> 00:02:32,386
No one understands us, Ruhi.

39
00:02:34,622 --> 00:02:36,290
"Just not today."

40
00:02:36,357 --> 00:02:37,691
Or any day!

41
00:02:40,093 --> 00:02:42,263
How can I be a hero
to the people...

42
00:02:43,497 --> 00:02:46,300
if I can't be around

43
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,369
any people?!

44
00:02:55,243 --> 00:02:56,444
Ha!

45
00:03:36,317 --> 00:03:37,518
Why?

46
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:40,421
Why do you look like... me?

47
00:03:40,888 --> 00:03:43,090
Uh, if anyone looks like someone,

48
00:03:43,190 --> 00:03:44,558
you look like me.

49
00:03:44,625 --> 00:03:46,260
So we must be...

50
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,461
-Twins?
-Twins.

51
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:53,966
W-wait, hold on.
You were bending...

52
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:55,307
O-oh, no, you-you didn't see...

53
00:03:55,403 --> 00:03:57,271
You were bending
all the elements!

54
00:03:57,371 --> 00:03:59,206
Me? Bend all four elements?

55
00:03:59,273 --> 00:04:00,974
The heat must be getting to you!

56
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:02,710
I don't understand.

57
00:04:02,776 --> 00:04:04,912
I thought I was the only one.

58
00:04:05,012 --> 00:04:06,514
"The only one"?

59
00:04:07,047 --> 00:04:09,249
-You mean, you can...
-Wait, I didn't say...

60
00:04:09,350 --> 00:04:10,384
Yes, you did.

61
00:04:10,484 --> 00:04:11,752
Are you really like me?

62
00:04:11,852 --> 00:04:13,754
No! I mean, no.

63
00:04:13,821 --> 00:04:14,755
No.

64
00:04:15,323 --> 00:04:17,991
Yeah, you are definitely lying.
You're not very good at it.

65
00:04:18,426 --> 00:04:20,461
I don't want any attention
from the Brigade.

66
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:23,464
Everyone is preparing
for the festival!

67
00:04:23,564 --> 00:04:24,498
It is just us.

68
00:04:24,598 --> 00:04:26,734
I promise I won't tell anyone.

69
00:04:28,268 --> 00:04:29,537
Which district are you from?

70
00:04:29,637 --> 00:04:31,505
I live here in the Compound.

71
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:33,441
Captain Karthik found me
three years ago

72
00:04:33,541 --> 00:04:35,008
and trains me in secret.

73
00:04:35,142 --> 00:04:37,378
I don't remember anything
before that.

74
00:04:37,811 --> 00:04:40,581
I don't remember
where I'm from either.

75
00:04:40,648 --> 00:04:41,815
Really?

76
00:04:41,915 --> 00:04:43,384
So we are twins!

77
00:04:43,484 --> 00:04:45,118
You can show me what you can do,

78
00:04:45,218 --> 00:04:46,454
I won't tell anyone.

79
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:49,890
Fine. It's just...

80
00:04:50,658 --> 00:04:52,659
I'm tired of being different.

81
00:04:53,661 --> 00:04:55,929
I wanna know
if there's anyone else like me.

82
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:07,875
Now show me the other elements.

83
00:05:07,975 --> 00:05:09,643
I... I have no idea

84
00:05:09,710 --> 00:05:10,750
what you're talking about.

85
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:12,913
Seriously,
you're a terrible liar.

86
00:05:13,013 --> 00:05:14,582
You say that
like it's a bad thing!

87
00:05:14,682 --> 00:05:16,517
Okay, I'll go first.

88
00:05:18,786 --> 00:05:19,887
So...

89
00:05:20,454 --> 00:05:22,456
are you really like me?

90
00:05:38,406 --> 00:05:40,007
Pavi, catch!

91
00:05:40,874 --> 00:05:42,976
I got it, Nisha!

92
00:05:53,887 --> 00:05:55,055
Did you...

93
00:05:55,155 --> 00:05:56,189
Yeah.

94
00:05:57,491 --> 00:05:58,626
Hi...

95
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:00,561
Nisha.

96
00:06:01,562 --> 00:06:02,730
Hi back...

97
00:06:03,831 --> 00:06:04,698
Pavi.

98
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,402
We loved playing catch.

99
00:06:08,502 --> 00:06:12,039
Well, Pavi, instead of catch,
how about a game of tag?

100
00:06:12,139 --> 00:06:13,641
Tag?

101
00:06:13,741 --> 00:06:15,261
I'm sorry, what is...

102
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:16,610
Tag! You're it!

103
00:06:20,948 --> 00:06:24,217
Oh, wow. Y-your leg.
How did I miss that?

104
00:06:24,284 --> 00:06:25,385
Are you okay?

105
00:06:25,453 --> 00:06:27,621
Oh, I was born this way.

106
00:06:28,589 --> 00:06:30,457
Ha!

107
00:06:30,558 --> 00:06:33,360
Now you're it!

108
00:06:43,103 --> 00:06:45,973
So... how are we both like this?

109
00:06:46,073 --> 00:06:47,707
Well, as long as I can remember,

110
00:06:47,775 --> 00:06:51,178
I've been secretly training
to be the Avatar.

111
00:06:51,779 --> 00:06:53,514
But if I'm the Avatar...

112
00:06:54,114 --> 00:06:55,248
what does that make you?

113
00:06:55,348 --> 00:06:56,817
Nisha!

114
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:58,852
Where are you?! I need to...

115
00:06:58,952 --> 00:07:00,454
Ow!

116
00:07:01,555 --> 00:07:03,123
Karthik, look!

117
00:07:03,223 --> 00:07:04,758
I have a twin!

118
00:07:10,831 --> 00:07:11,899
Pavi,

119
00:07:11,965 --> 00:07:14,468
Nisha told me quite a lot
about you.

120
00:07:14,602 --> 00:07:16,436
Do you see my cup of tea?

121
00:07:17,104 --> 00:07:20,040
Would you mind showing me
a little of your abilities?

122
00:07:20,941 --> 00:07:23,711
I swear to you,
I mean you no harm.

123
00:07:26,814 --> 00:07:27,781
It's okay.

124
00:07:47,034 --> 00:07:48,602
Two Avatars?

125
00:07:48,669 --> 00:07:52,372
A-are you going to make me join

126
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:54,074
the Bending Brigade?

127
00:07:54,742 --> 00:07:56,109
What you are

128
00:07:56,744 --> 00:07:59,747
is more important
than the entire Brigade.

129
00:07:59,847 --> 00:08:01,515
Both you and Nisha.

130
00:08:01,615 --> 00:08:03,183
I've had to hide like you.

131
00:08:03,283 --> 00:08:05,118
The Brigade thinks
I'm Captain Karthik's

132
00:08:05,218 --> 00:08:06,153
bending-less assistant.

133
00:08:06,253 --> 00:08:07,955
But soon they'll know the truth.

134
00:08:08,021 --> 00:08:10,190
Only a few people know
Nisha's secret.

135
00:08:10,290 --> 00:08:13,293
And I guess that now means
you do too, Jae.

136
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,528
Uh-huh.

137
00:08:14,662 --> 00:08:16,930
Uh, I am processing
all of this...

138
00:08:17,030 --> 00:08:19,199
f-f-fantastically.

139
00:08:19,299 --> 00:08:21,702
I can't be an Avatar.

140
00:08:22,069 --> 00:08:23,436
I'm no warrior.

141
00:08:23,971 --> 00:08:26,006
And the last one
doomed the world,

142
00:08:26,073 --> 00:08:27,307
didn't she?

143
00:08:27,841 --> 00:08:30,110
Korra wasn't a normal Avatar.

144
00:08:30,210 --> 00:08:32,145
Most recorded history is lost,

145
00:08:32,212 --> 00:08:34,881
but what we have found
points to...

146
00:08:36,515 --> 00:08:39,687
Avatar Korra caused
the Cataclysm.

147
00:08:39,753 --> 00:08:42,823
Because of the destruction
Korra wrought,

148
00:08:42,923 --> 00:08:45,358
the Avatar became
an enemy of the world.

149
00:08:45,793 --> 00:08:47,561
Regardless of what Korra did,

150
00:08:47,661 --> 00:08:50,564
I believe in a more hopeful
version of the Avatar

151
00:08:50,664 --> 00:08:52,600
than the Seven Havens do.

152
00:08:52,933 --> 00:08:55,102
For thousands of years,

153
00:08:55,235 --> 00:08:57,938
the Avatar reincarnated
again and again

154
00:08:58,038 --> 00:08:59,740
to defend the people
of the world,

155
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:02,676
no matter their class
or their station.

156
00:09:02,776 --> 00:09:05,012
That's the kind of Avatar
I wanna be.

157
00:09:05,078 --> 00:09:07,581
I had no idea there was more
to the legend.

158
00:09:07,715 --> 00:09:09,249
Most people don't.

159
00:09:10,017 --> 00:09:12,552
Have there ever been
twin Avatars?

160
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:14,554
Never before you two.

161
00:09:14,955 --> 00:09:17,457
But how else can we explain
your likeness to Nisha

162
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:18,726
and your abilities?

163
00:09:18,792 --> 00:09:21,128
You never considered
you're an Avatar?

164
00:09:21,228 --> 00:09:24,231
I guess I always feared I was...

165
00:09:24,732 --> 00:09:26,199
but hoped I wasn't.

166
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:27,567
Join us.

167
00:09:28,001 --> 00:09:29,036
Train with your sister

168
00:09:29,102 --> 00:09:30,971
and become
a fully-fledged Avatar.

169
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:35,108
But you don't need me,
you have an Avatar!

170
00:09:35,542 --> 00:09:37,845
She's me, but not a mess!

171
00:09:37,945 --> 00:09:39,980
I spend my time collecting rocks

172
00:09:40,113 --> 00:09:42,515
and introducing myself to bugs!

173
00:09:43,183 --> 00:09:44,417
I'm a nobody.

174
00:09:44,818 --> 00:09:45,886
Just a fluke.

175
00:09:46,453 --> 00:09:49,556
I learned a long time ago
not to believe in coincidences.

176
00:09:49,623 --> 00:09:50,624
Pavi, listen to me.

177
00:09:50,758 --> 00:09:52,660
You are important.

178
00:09:52,793 --> 00:09:55,829
Pavi, together
we can be unstoppable.

179
00:09:55,963 --> 00:09:57,798
We can fix the world.

180
00:09:58,799 --> 00:10:00,801
Okay, well, this has been fun,

181
00:10:00,901 --> 00:10:04,471
but I should really get back
to my cave.

182
00:10:04,571 --> 00:10:06,339
Geet and I have big dinner plans.

183
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:13,513
By the Havens...

184
00:10:52,953 --> 00:10:56,056
Yuy, get those water barrels
to the launching bay!

185
00:10:56,156 --> 00:10:58,792
Chung, are you an earth bender
or are your feet made of mud?

186
00:10:58,926 --> 00:10:59,760
Let's move!

187
00:10:59,860 --> 00:11:01,862
Go, your Haven needs you!

188
00:11:01,962 --> 00:11:03,196
-You heard the captain!
-Sir,

189
00:11:03,263 --> 00:11:04,794
I request to join my squad
out on the front.

190
00:11:04,798 --> 00:11:07,534
Jae, what you've learned
can never be spoken about.

191
00:11:07,634 --> 00:11:10,137
All I want right now
is to help my people.

192
00:11:11,238 --> 00:11:12,039
Good.

193
00:11:12,139 --> 00:11:13,340
Now get to your squad,

194
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:14,441
Airbender!

195
00:11:16,443 --> 00:11:19,046
Take Pavi to your room
where it's safe.

196
00:11:21,614 --> 00:11:23,316
Wait! Captain!

197
00:11:23,416 --> 00:11:25,318
Captain, I'm ready.

198
00:11:25,452 --> 00:11:27,287
Absolutely not, Nisha.

199
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:29,790
Isn't this what you've been
training me for?

200
00:11:29,923 --> 00:11:31,458
To save the Haven?

201
00:11:31,591 --> 00:11:33,160
The Brigade
has this storm covered.

202
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:34,627
Ellora's not ready for you.

203
00:11:34,728 --> 00:11:37,030
They don't know me! Or Pavi!

204
00:11:37,130 --> 00:11:38,631
If they just got a chance...

205
00:11:38,732 --> 00:11:41,234
Introducing you
in the middle of a disaster

206
00:11:41,301 --> 00:11:43,170
will only feed the chaos.

207
00:11:43,270 --> 00:11:44,604
End of discussion.

208
00:11:44,671 --> 00:11:45,505
But, Karthik...

209
00:11:45,638 --> 00:11:46,639
"Captain."

210
00:11:46,774 --> 00:11:49,009
Remember your place, Nisha.

211
00:12:03,256 --> 00:12:04,257
Ugh!

212
00:12:06,326 --> 00:12:07,460
Nisha, let's head back.

213
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:08,829
We're going.

214
00:12:08,962 --> 00:12:11,031
Right, going somewhere safe.

215
00:12:11,164 --> 00:12:12,299
Probably underground.

216
00:12:12,365 --> 00:12:13,500
Oh, I know a great hole.

217
00:12:13,633 --> 00:12:16,336
-No! We're going out there!
-Oh, yeah, well,

218
00:12:16,436 --> 00:12:19,506
didn't your teacher-dad-boss
just say that's forbidden?

219
00:12:19,606 --> 00:12:20,841
I know, but...

220
00:12:20,974 --> 00:12:22,976
I just... feel in my heart

221
00:12:23,076 --> 00:12:25,779
this is what the Avatar
is supposed to do.

222
00:12:27,848 --> 00:12:29,016
Don't you?

223
00:12:33,353 --> 00:12:35,188
Come with me.

224
00:12:35,322 --> 00:12:37,424
Let's save Ellora together.

225
00:12:38,491 --> 00:12:41,561
Nisha, this is your life,
not mine.

226
00:12:41,661 --> 00:12:42,930
What are you saying?

227
00:12:43,030 --> 00:12:45,265
You haven't seen Ellora like me.

228
00:12:45,365 --> 00:12:48,235
They think the Avatar
is a monster!

229
00:12:48,368 --> 00:12:50,637
Is that how you see me?

230
00:12:50,737 --> 00:12:52,539
No! How could I?

231
00:12:53,006 --> 00:12:55,042
But... I'm no hero.

232
00:12:55,142 --> 00:12:57,878
I was just trying to help
my friend Sang,

233
00:12:57,978 --> 00:13:00,113
and then my whole life
fell apart.

234
00:13:00,981 --> 00:13:03,216
I'm not an Avatar.

235
00:13:05,485 --> 00:13:07,654
I've been alone for so long.

236
00:13:07,754 --> 00:13:10,924
I thought I found someone
who finally understands.

237
00:13:11,024 --> 00:13:13,226
Someone who could be family.

238
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:14,828
I was wrong.

239
00:13:14,928 --> 00:13:17,630
Nisha, no. Please, wait!

240
00:13:26,239 --> 00:13:28,108
This isn't our world, Geet.

241
00:13:28,775 --> 00:13:30,477
And it's never gonna be.

242
00:13:35,348 --> 00:13:37,117
Quick! Close the doors!

243
00:13:37,217 --> 00:13:38,852
I have a baby!

244
00:13:38,919 --> 00:13:40,854
-Get inside!
-Get to shelter!

245
00:13:45,692 --> 00:13:46,960
Come on! Come on!

246
00:13:47,094 --> 00:13:48,428
We gotta keep going!

247
00:13:50,130 --> 00:13:51,131
Oh, no!

248
00:13:56,203 --> 00:13:58,171
They need my help!

249
00:14:12,152 --> 00:14:13,120
I did it, Ruhi!

250
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:14,854
Ugh!

251
00:14:16,189 --> 00:14:17,824
Ah!

252
00:14:28,335 --> 00:14:30,437
I know, Geet.

253
00:14:30,503 --> 00:14:33,173
But Nisha and the Brigade
have it covered.

254
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:45,218
Hey! Are you okay?

255
00:14:45,652 --> 00:14:47,854
Are... aren't you scared?

256
00:14:47,955 --> 00:14:50,390
Oh, I am terrified.

257
00:14:50,490 --> 00:14:52,993
But I can help people,
so I'm out here.

258
00:14:53,426 --> 00:14:54,461
Ulan!

259
00:15:00,367 --> 00:15:02,402
Ugh. Don't you start.

260
00:15:06,206 --> 00:15:09,042
Those kids
are amazing together.

261
00:15:09,509 --> 00:15:10,910
So brave.

262
00:15:11,011 --> 00:15:12,879
Maybe with Nisha,

263
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:15,983
this could all be
a little less scary.

264
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:29,162
Brace the gates!

265
00:15:44,177 --> 00:15:46,546
Nice of you to join us,
squad leader!

266
00:15:46,646 --> 00:15:48,381
Is everyone okay?

267
00:15:59,726 --> 00:16:01,461
Let's join Commander Bountan.

268
00:16:13,073 --> 00:16:14,007
Commander!

269
00:16:24,951 --> 00:16:26,953
We're doomed!

270
00:16:31,691 --> 00:16:33,793
How are we gonna survive?

271
00:17:01,321 --> 00:17:03,323
What nightmare is this?!

272
00:17:10,163 --> 00:17:12,531
Commander, what are your orders?

273
00:17:13,133 --> 00:17:14,834
Run!

274
00:17:15,167 --> 00:17:16,435
Commander!

275
00:17:20,339 --> 00:17:22,242
Get back, you demon!

276
00:17:45,465 --> 00:17:47,134
Brigade, regroup on me!

277
00:17:47,667 --> 00:17:51,104
Whatever this thing is,
I need defensive barriers now!

278
00:17:51,204 --> 00:17:53,506
You heard our Captain, let's go!

279
00:18:30,042 --> 00:18:32,912
Hi!

280
00:18:33,012 --> 00:18:34,747
I thought you were scared.

281
00:18:34,847 --> 00:18:35,948
I was!

282
00:18:36,082 --> 00:18:37,450
I still am!

283
00:18:37,584 --> 00:18:38,651
But I'm here with you.

284
00:18:38,751 --> 00:18:39,919
Ah!

285
00:18:40,019 --> 00:18:41,288
What is that thing?!

286
00:18:46,593 --> 00:18:48,961
I don't know,
but it either likes us

287
00:18:49,061 --> 00:18:50,997
or really hates us.

288
00:18:55,502 --> 00:18:56,903
How's your earth bending?

289
00:18:57,003 --> 00:18:58,571
It's my best element!

290
00:18:58,671 --> 00:19:00,740
Same! Let's go together!

291
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:33,640
Uh... Pavi?

292
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:35,808
Now I'm scared.

293
00:19:36,142 --> 00:19:38,478
Me too.
But extra more scared now.

294
00:19:45,818 --> 00:19:48,388
-What's going on?
-Where are we?

295
00:20:09,476 --> 00:20:11,678
Is it done?

296
00:20:11,778 --> 00:20:13,246
Did it pass?

297
00:20:16,349 --> 00:20:17,917
Search for survivors.

298
00:20:18,017 --> 00:20:19,719
I'm gonna do a perimeter check.

299
00:20:24,023 --> 00:20:25,892
It's over, I think.

300
00:20:25,992 --> 00:20:27,827
What was that scary zappy thing?

301
00:20:27,894 --> 00:20:31,331
No idea. It looked like
it was made of... energy?

302
00:20:31,431 --> 00:20:33,600
Ugh.

303
00:20:36,869 --> 00:20:37,937
Hi.

304
00:20:42,542 --> 00:20:45,678
Captain! Uh,
we were just out for a...

305
00:20:45,778 --> 00:20:47,780
Whatever
that nightmare was,

306
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:50,483
we have you two
to thank for its demise.

307
00:20:50,550 --> 00:20:51,784
Well done, Nisha.

308
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:56,255
You're clearly not the "mess"
you think you are, Pavi.

309
00:20:56,356 --> 00:20:58,558
Captain Karthik,
we found the commander!

310
00:20:58,658 --> 00:21:01,561
Go back to the Brigade Compound,
both of you.

311
00:21:03,330 --> 00:21:04,331
Come on!

312
00:21:05,465 --> 00:21:06,799
Ugh.

313
00:21:15,708 --> 00:21:18,811
Commander, it's me. Karthik.

314
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:22,214
It is coming.

315
00:21:22,315 --> 00:21:23,450
What's coming?

316
00:21:25,818 --> 00:21:28,321
Commander!
Somebody bring a stretcher!

317
00:21:29,589 --> 00:21:31,358
Did you see the old guy's eyes?

318
00:21:31,458 --> 00:21:32,625
What happened to him?

319
00:21:32,725 --> 00:21:34,461
No clue, but I bet it's tied

320
00:21:34,594 --> 00:21:36,028
to the energy monster.

321
00:21:36,128 --> 00:21:37,229
Let's get out of here,

322
00:21:37,330 --> 00:21:39,699
or Karthik really
will get mad at us.

323
00:21:44,437 --> 00:21:46,706
Whoo! That was amazing, right?

324
00:21:46,773 --> 00:21:47,674
Yeah!

325
00:21:47,774 --> 00:21:48,941
Oh, uh...

326
00:21:49,075 --> 00:21:51,711
Does "amazing" not mean
what I think it means?

327
00:21:54,781 --> 00:21:57,249
We have to be ready
if that thing comes back.

328
00:21:57,316 --> 00:21:58,585
What do you say, Pavi?

329
00:21:58,685 --> 00:21:59,986
Are we in this together?

330
00:22:00,887 --> 00:22:01,888
For now,

331
00:22:02,254 --> 00:22:05,024
can we start with me
just being your, um...

332
00:22:05,892 --> 00:22:06,926
friend?

333
00:22:07,994 --> 00:22:09,028
Better idea.

334
00:22:09,596 --> 00:22:11,297
Do you wanna be...

335
00:22:11,931 --> 00:22:13,299
my sister?

336
00:22:15,001 --> 00:22:16,436
Sisters it is.

337
00:22:24,444 --> 00:22:25,344
That's right, Geet,

338
00:22:25,445 --> 00:22:27,814
you have a cat-sister now too!

339
00:22:27,914 --> 00:22:31,150
Or would it be cat-cousins?

340
00:22:32,318 --> 00:22:33,686
We have a lot to figure out

341
00:22:33,820 --> 00:22:35,087
including...

342
00:22:36,589 --> 00:22:37,857
Which cat-monkey is faster?

343
00:22:37,957 --> 00:22:39,692
Race you back to the Compound!

344
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:41,861
Let's scramble, Geet!
